Role Mapping: Technology to Functional Role

Purpose:
  Maps each technology to its primary functional role.

Mappings:
  languages:
    go: Backend
    rust: Backend
    java: Backend
    php: Backend
    python: Backend
    csharp: Backend
    cpp: Backend/Systems
    typescript: Backend or Frontend
    javascript: Frontend or Backend
    swift: Mobile
    kotlin: Mobile
    ruby: Backend

  frameworks:
    react: Frontend
    vue: Frontend
    angular: Frontend
    svelte: Frontend
    nextjs: Frontend
    flutter: Mobile
    react-native: Mobile
    swiftui: Mobile
    kotlin-multiplatform: Mobile
    spring-boot: Backend
    django: Backend
    fastapi: Backend
    express: Backend
    nestjs: Backend
    dotnet: Backend
    laravel: Backend
    symfony: Backend

  databases:
    postgresql: Database
    mongodb: Database
    redis: Database/Infrastructure
    mysql: Database
    cassandra: Database
    elasticsearch: Database/Infrastructure

  platforms:
    docker: DevOps
    kubernetes: DevOps
    aws: DevOps
    gcp: DevOps
    azure: DevOps
    terraform: DevOps

  messaging:
    kafka: Backend/DevOps
    rabbitmq: Backend/DevOps
    nats: Backend/DevOps

  cross-cutting:
    testing: QA
    security: Security
    architecture: Architect
    observability: DevOps

Rules:
  [RM1] Each technology MUST have exactly one primary role.
  [RM2] Technologies MAY have secondary roles for cross-cutting concerns.
  [RM3] Role assignment MUST consider case context.
  [RM4] Ambiguous assignments MUST be flagged for human review.

State: +
